│ patch_description        │ Improve the high-dirt revisit operation by selecting the detour insertion point globally  │
│                          │ instead of from only 20 random route positions.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Operation 4 is intended to add visits to a currently expensive cell. Its effectiveness is │
│                          │ dominated by detour length: sampling only 20 positions often chooses a location far from  │
│                          │ the target even when the route already passes adjacent to it elsewhere. Scanning the      │
│                          │ existing route for the minimum APSP distance finds the cheapest valid round-trip detour,  │
│                          │ allowing more frequent revisits to high-contribution cells within the length budget.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Also narrow Op4 target selection from the top 10% of cells to the top O(N) cells. Since   │
│                          │ Op4 now finds the cheapest insertion point exactly, concentrating on the most costly      │
│                          │ cells produces stronger score-improving insertions while retaining randomness among       │
│                          │ several candidates.                                                                       │
