│ patch_name               │ gap_aware_detours                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Improve operation 4 (targeted detour insertion) by always considering an insertion point  │
│                          │ at the temporal midpoint of the target cell's largest current revisit gap.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The dirt contribution of a cell is proportional to the sum of squared revisit intervals.  │
│                          │ When adding an extra visit to a target cell, placing it in the middle of its largest      │
│                          │ interval gives the largest direct reduction in that cell's dirt term. The existing        │
│                          │ implementation chooses only random route positions, so it often inserts a useful detour   │
│                          │ at a poor time in the cycle.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This change retains the random samples for route diversification, but adds one            │
│                          │ deterministic high-value candidate. It uses the visit-time buffer already computed by     │
│                          │ `calculate_score_full`, including correct handling of the cyclic interval between the     │
│                          │ last and first visit.                                                                     │
