│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ faster_targeting_and_better_segment_repair                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current search spends a substantial fraction of its limited time sorting all cells    │
│                          │ whenever it chooses a dirt target, despite only needing a random element from the         │
│                          │ highest-contribution prefix. Replacing the full sort with `nth_element` preserves the     │
│                          │ intended target distribution while reducing this operation from O(N^2 log N) to expected  │
│                          │ O(N^2).                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, the shortest-path-through-target operation is currently restricted to       │
│                          │ replacing a segment of at most 20 moves. This makes it unable to repair the long revisit  │
│                          │ intervals that dominate the dirt objective, especially after the route has grown through  │
│                          │ detours. Increasing its replacement window allows the operator to replace a large poor    │
│                          │ section with two shortest paths through an important dirty cell; it can both improve      │
│                          │ visit frequency and remove inefficient route sections. The length constraint and          │
│                          │ simulated annealing acceptance still protect against invalid or consistently harmful      │
│                          │ replacements.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Finally, operation 1 currently allocates and scans the entire route to find an immediate  │
│                          │ backtrack pair. Sampling several positions finds removable backtracks cheaply, allowing   │
│                          │ materially more score evaluations during the same time budget.                            │
│ num_applied              │ 4                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0275                                                                                   │
