│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ exact_target_visit_insertion                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Operation 4 selects a target square with high current dirt contribution, but the current  │
│                          │ implementation samples only 20 route positions when choosing where to insert the detour.  │
│                          │ Every target square is necessarily already visited by the valid route, so an exact        │
│                          │ occurrence always exists and permits a cost-2 local wiggle. Missing it causes             │
│                          │ unnecessarily long detours, consumes route length, and dilutes all visit frequencies.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Scan the route coordinates to find an occurrence of the target square, using reservoir    │
│                          │ sampling among occurrences to preserve phase diversity. This makes operation 4            │
│                          │ consistently add the intended cheap extra visit to the important target.                  │
