│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ peak_gap_targeting                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Prioritize cells with a long worst revisit interval in addition to their existing total   │
│                          │ dirt contribution. The benefit of adding a visit is dominated by splitting a long gap:    │
│                          │ the dirt accumulated over a gap grows quadratically with its duration. The existing       │
│                          │ target score only stores the sum over all gaps, which can over-prioritize cells that are  │
│                          │ already visited often. Store each cell's maximum cyclic gap during scoring and blend its  │
│                          │ corresponding dirt term into target selection. This affects both detour insertion and     │
│                          │ target-based subpath replacement while retaining part of the original robust              │
│                          │ total-contribution signal.                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
