│ patch_name               │ phase_aware_detours                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Improve Op4’s insertion-point selection. Previously it selected the sampled position with │
│                          │ the shortest detour to the dirty target, ignoring where in the target cell’s cleaning     │
│                          │ cycle that new visit occurs. A slightly longer detour can be substantially better if it   │
│                          │ splits the target’s largest revisit gap.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The added helper evaluates the target cell’s exact periodic dirt term after a proposed    │
│                          │ closed detour. Op4 still limits itself to positions whose detour is close to the shortest │
│                          │ sampled detour, avoiding wasteful route growth, but selects among them by the predicted   │
│                          │ reduction in the target’s weighted average contribution. This preserves the cheap sampled │
│                          │ neighborhood while making targeted insertions phase-aware.                                │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
