│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ flatroute_sa                                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This redesign uses a flattened graph architecture instead of coordinate-heavy global      │
│                          │ structures. It precomputes all-pairs shortest-path first moves in compact arrays,         │
│                          │ represents routes as strings plus flattened cell IDs, and evaluates dirtiness in one      │
│                          │ linear scan using first/last visit timestamps and gap accumulation rather than per-cell   │
│                          │ visit vectors.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search is organized around a compact simulated-annealing engine with modular mutation │
│                          │ operators: local detours, cancellation, shortest-path compression, path reversal,         │
│                          │ targeted high-dirt revisits, and targeted segment replacement. Several weighted           │
│                          │ randomized DFS tours are evaluated before optimization to provide a better initial state. │
│                          │ This substantially reduces allocation overhead and route-evaluation cost, allowing more   │
│                          │ meaningful search iterations within the time limit.                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.1010                                                                                   │
