│ patch_name               │ flat_route_sa                                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This redesign replaces the heavyweight `PathData` copying/scoring flow with a flat        │
│                          │ route-state architecture:                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Routes are stored as compact direction bytes rather than characters.                    │
│                          │ - Board cells are represented by flat integer IDs.                                        │
│                          │ - Legal transitions and APSP first-step directions are precomputed in flat arrays.        │
│                          │ - Scoring no longer allocates or clears per-cell visit vectors. It computes cyclic visit  │
│                          │ gaps in one route scan using first/last visit timestamps and per-cell accumulated terms.  │
│                          │ - Candidate states only copy the move sequence; coordinates and score metadata are        │
│                          │ rebuilt only after a successful proposal.                                                 │
│                          │ - Backtrack deletion samples valid removable pairs directly instead of constructing a     │
│                          │ full candidate-index list.                                                                │
│                          │ - Closed-loop reversal is retained as a legal structural edit, avoiding invalid arbitrary │
│                          │ segment reversals.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This substantially reduces allocation, copying, pointer chasing, and scorer overhead,     │
│                          │ allowing many more local-search iterations within the same time budget.                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
